---
description: |
  The bounded, round-trip-inverting read-back for the ocsf class
  tables: the leg every attest-verify walk reads its window through.

  WHY THIS OPERATOR EXISTS (2026-11-05 detection-plane write outage,
  .scratch/ocsf-ddl-audit/laps/sre-core-crash-report.md): the walks'
  old shape — `from_clickhouse table=...` plus a TQL-side
  `where time > now() - 90m` — never reached the server. The
  from_clickhouse pushdown only forwards filters ClickHouse can
  evaluate exactly like Tenzir, and time bounds qualify only as
  comparisons against foldable literals (the vendored optimization
  reference: "Expressions that consist of literals only ... are
  computed ahead of time"; now() is not one) — so every walk's every
  retry ran `SELECT * FROM ocsf.<class> WHERE
  event.attestation_list IS NOT NULL ...` as an UNBOUNDED full-table
  scan (system.query_log, live evidence: Process_Activity = 86.4M
  rows / 12.9 GiB per attempt; three concurrent scans on one replica
  at 21:34Z). The replica saturation then 30s-timeout'd every write
  pipeline in the fleet. Reading through `sql` mode instead pins the
  window into the executed query itself (the sql mode contract:
  "Tenzir sends the query as is and does not rewrite it"), and the
  prefilter keeps the attested-rows-only scan shape the walk needs.

  WHY THE RECONSTRUCTION: sql mode returns the raw columns — the
  catch-all reconstruction is table mode's ("The sql mode and tables
  without a catch-all column return the columns as they are"), and
  verify needs records, not rows. Each arm below rebuilds the event
  exactly as table mode would: the catch-all parsed back (the
  reference: "Tenzir infers the types of JSON values like parse_json
  does"), every typed column re-merged at its path (the column wins
  over the catch-all, shallow per parent — TQL merge is a shallow
  second-wins spread), null nullable columns as null fields, JSON
  columns as records. Lab-verified byte-identical to table mode on
  every walked class shape (2026-11-05, engine v6.20.1 against
  ClickHouse 26.10.3.7 with the production DDL), so verify's input
  contract — the stored-shape record — is unchanged from the table-mode
  era.

  THE STRIP: the last leg calls
  homelab::record_integrity::ocsf::strip, which inverts the column
  artifacts the catch-all reconstruction injects for fields the
  pre-INSERT record lacked (severity_id's DEFAULT 0, null nullable
  columns, the emptied parents), so the records verify.tql receives
  reconstruct the stamp-side hash input. That inversion is a separate
  operator so the package test harness can drive it with fixtures —
  this operator needs a live ClickHouse and is proven by the lap's
  lab evidence instead.

  The json_type_escape_dots_in_keys setting is required in sql mode:
  the catch-all write escapes literal dotted keys, and table mode
  re-enables the setting on read — "With sql, add SETTINGS
  json_type_escape_dots_in_keys=1 to your query. Otherwise,
  ClickHouse returns escaped keys such as 'a%2Eb'" (from_clickhouse
  reference). k8s-audit annotations and similar residue keys keep
  their dots on the way back through this leg.
args:
  named:
    - name: table
      type: string
      description: The ocsf class table to read, e.g. "ocsf.API_Activity".
    - name: window
      type: int
      default: 90
      description: |
        The rolling read-back window in MINUTES. Must stay wider than
        the walk cadence (90 vs the hourly walk: the 30-minute overlap
        gives every record 1-2 covering walks and swallows the ~90s
        late-write budget of the stamping windows).
    - name: host
      type: string
      default: "clickhouse-tenzir.tenzir.svc.cluster.local"
    - name: port
      type: int
      default: 9000
    - name: user
      type: string
      default: "tenzir"
    - name: password
      type: secret
    - name: tls
      type: bool
      default: false
---

from_clickhouse sql=f"SELECT * FROM {$table} WHERE event.attestation_list IS NOT NULL AND time > now() - INTERVAL {$window} MINUTE SETTINGS json_type_escape_dots_in_keys=1",
  host=$host,
  port=$port,
  user=$user,
  password=$password,
  tls=$tls

// The raw row: typed columns at top level (dotted names as literal
// fields), event/unmapped as one-line JSON text. Rebuild per table,
// mirroring the store's hand-DDL column set (config/10-startup-scripts
// .xml) — a new typed column pairs with its arm here, same lap, or the
// read-back silently drops the field from verify's hash input.
_ev = parse_json(event)
_unmapped_raw = unmapped
_time_col = time
_cuid_col = class_uid
_sev_col = severity_id
match $table {
  "ocsf.API_Activity" => {
    this = {
      ..._ev,
      actor: merge(_ev.actor?, {user: merge(_ev.actor?.user?, {name: this["actor.user.name"]})}),
      api: merge(_ev.api?, {operation: this["api.operation"]}),
      metadata: merge(_ev.metadata?, {product: merge(_ev.metadata?.product?, {name: this["metadata.product.name"]})}),
      src_endpoint: merge(_ev.src_endpoint?, {ip: this["src_endpoint.ip"]}),
      time: _time_col,
      class_uid: _cuid_col,
      severity_id: _sev_col,
      unmapped: parse_json(_unmapped_raw),
    }
  }
  "ocsf.Authentication" => {
    this = {
      ..._ev,
      actor: merge(_ev.actor?, {user: merge(_ev.actor?.user?, {name: this["actor.user.name"]})}),
      metadata: merge(_ev.metadata?, {product: merge(_ev.metadata?.product?, {name: this["metadata.product.name"]})}),
      src_endpoint: merge(_ev.src_endpoint?, {ip: this["src_endpoint.ip"]}),
      time: _time_col,
      class_uid: _cuid_col,
      severity_id: _sev_col,
      status_id: this["status_id"],
      unmapped: parse_json(_unmapped_raw),
    }
  }
  "ocsf.Account_Change" => {
    this = {
      ..._ev,
      actor: merge(_ev.actor?, {user: merge(_ev.actor?.user?, {name: this["actor.user.name"]})}),
      metadata: merge(_ev.metadata?, {product: merge(_ev.metadata?.product?, {name: this["metadata.product.name"]})}),
      src_endpoint: merge(_ev.src_endpoint?, {ip: this["src_endpoint.ip"]}),
      time: _time_col,
      class_uid: _cuid_col,
      severity_id: _sev_col,
      unmapped: parse_json(_unmapped_raw),
    }
  }
  "ocsf.Detection_Finding" => {
    this = {
      ..._ev,
      metadata: merge(_ev.metadata?, {product: merge(_ev.metadata?.product?, {name: this["metadata.product.name"]})}),
      finding_info: merge(_ev.finding_info?, {title: this["finding_info.title"], uid: this["finding_info.uid"]}),
      time: _time_col,
      class_uid: _cuid_col,
      severity_id: _sev_col,
      status_id: this["status_id"],
      uid: this["uid"],
      rule_id: this["rule_id"],
      subject_kind: this["subject_kind"],
      subject_name: this["subject_name"],
      subject_namespace: this["subject_namespace"],
      unmapped: parse_json(_unmapped_raw),
    }
  }
  "ocsf.Vulnerability_Finding" => {
    this = {
      ..._ev,
      metadata: merge(_ev.metadata?, {product: merge(_ev.metadata?.product?, {name: this["metadata.product.name"]})}),
      finding_info: merge(_ev.finding_info?, {title: this["finding_info.title"]}),
      time: _time_col,
      class_uid: _cuid_col,
      severity_id: _sev_col,
      unmapped: parse_json(_unmapped_raw),
    }
  }
  "ocsf.Base_Event" => {
    this = {
      ..._ev,
      device: merge(_ev.device?, {hostname: this["device.hostname"]}),
      metadata: merge(_ev.metadata?, {product: merge(_ev.metadata?.product?, {name: this["metadata.product.name"]})}),
      time: _time_col,
      class_uid: _cuid_col,
      severity_id: _sev_col,
      class_name: this["class_name"],
      activity_id: this["activity_id"],
      unmapped: parse_json(_unmapped_raw),
    }
  }
  "ocsf.Process_Activity" => {
    this = {
      ..._ev,
      process: merge(_ev.process?, {path: this["process.path"]}),
      device: merge(_ev.device?, {hostname: this["device.hostname"]}),
      metadata: merge(_ev.metadata?, {product: merge(_ev.metadata?.product?, {name: this["metadata.product.name"]})}),
      time: _time_col,
      class_uid: _cuid_col,
      severity_id: _sev_col,
      activity_id: this["activity_id"],
      unmapped: parse_json(_unmapped_raw),
    }
  }
  "ocsf.File_System_Activity" => {
    this = {
      ..._ev,
      file: merge(_ev.file?, {path: this["file.path"], xattributes: merge(_ev.file?.xattributes?, {permission: this["file.xattributes.permission"]})}),
      actor: merge(_ev.actor?, {process: merge(_ev.actor?.process?, {path: this["actor.process.path"], container: merge(_ev.actor?.process?.container?, {name: this["actor.process.container.name"]})})}),
      device: merge(_ev.device?, {hostname: this["device.hostname"]}),
      metadata: merge(_ev.metadata?, {product: merge(_ev.metadata?.product?, {name: this["metadata.product.name"]})}),
      time: _time_col,
      class_uid: _cuid_col,
      severity_id: _sev_col,
      unmapped: parse_json(_unmapped_raw),
    }
  }
  "ocsf.Network_Activity" => {
    this = {
      ..._ev,
      src_endpoint: merge(_ev.src_endpoint?, {ip: this["src_endpoint.ip"]}),
      dst_endpoint: merge(_ev.dst_endpoint?, {ip: this["dst_endpoint.ip"]}),
      traffic: merge(_ev.traffic?, {bytes: this["traffic.bytes"]}),
      metadata: merge(_ev.metadata?, {product: merge(_ev.metadata?.product?, {name: this["metadata.product.name"]})}),
      time: _time_col,
      class_uid: _cuid_col,
      severity_id: _sev_col,
      unmapped: parse_json(_unmapped_raw),
    }
  }
  _ => {
    // An unmapped table would mean the walked class set drifted from
    // this operator's arm set; fail loud rather than verify against a
    // broken reconstruction.
    assert false, message=f"record_integrity::ocsf::read: no reconstruction arm for table {$table}"
  }
}

homelab::record_integrity::ocsf::strip
